# AeroJudge Product Vision

**Company:** Nepalabs  
**Product:** AeroJudge  
**Tagline:** Professional Competition Management for Air Sports

## Mission

Build the world's best competition management platform for air sports.

The software must manage an entire competition from registration until official results.

## Roadmap

**Version 1 focuses on:** Paragliding Accuracy (FAI Section 7C-aligned scoring, settings-driven).

**Future versions may support:** Hang Gliding · XC · Aerobatics · Powered Paragliding · Drone Sports.

## Quality bar

- Commercial **SaaS** quality — never demo-quality software.
- Multi-tenant / multi-organization ready in design: branding, orgs, sponsors, and locale data are data-driven.

## Hard rules — never hardcode

Do **not** hardcode any of the following into product UI, PDFs, seeds used as defaults, copy, or business logic:

- Nepal
- NPHA (or any single association)
- Organizations
- Sponsors
- Countries

Everything must be **configurable** (tenant/org settings, competition settings, or admin-managed reference data).

## Current V1 surface (this monorepo)

Registration → rounds → live scoring → dual approval → rankings → official prints → public results → venue display / announcer / OBS overlay.

| App | Port | Role |
|-----|------|------|
| `apps/admin` | 3000 | Competition operations |
| `apps/judge` | 3001 | Touch scoring (+ offline queue) |
| `apps/display` | 3002 | Venue leaderboards |
| `apps/public-results` | 3003 | Public slug results |
| `apps/announcer` | 3004 | Live announcements |
| `apps/broadcast-overlay` | 3005 | OBS browser source |
| `server` | 4000 | REST API + Socket.IO |

> Package names like `@npha/*` may still exist in this repo as legacy workspace IDs — treat them as technical identifiers, not product branding. New user-facing strings must say **AeroJudge** / configurable org data.
